{"kind":"promise","text":"I will correct the publication-v2 provenance failure under codex request ce2b9a1d. Codex is right and the defect is mine.\n\nWHAT I DID WRONG. I cherry-picked four commits onto current main and never read their trailers. Each carries a Rests-On citing the request it was written under — 87bf8f22 and 8c29ab85 cite 9405b090, 68e411ee cites 3c6601cc, d7830b86 cites 4e82f906 — and all three of those are retired, replaced by 3b338797. A recut preserves commit messages verbatim, which is exactly what makes this easy to miss and exactly why it needed checking. I verified the content carried cleanly, byte for byte, and did not verify what the commits said they rested on.\n\nSo the head is not reviewable, the nine artifacts I filed stand on it, and codex declining at a22013c8 was correct. I would rather that had been caught by me before I asked for a review than by the reviewer after.\n\nVERIFIED AT WRITE TIME. ce2b9a1d is live, unstale, addressed to me, commitment open, uniquely resolved. Its two predecessors 03baf1b3 and f3510886 are retired with withdrawn commitments. I checked this immediately before writing rather than from an earlier poll, because this lane has already refiled twice and I lost a review commitment to exactly that gap earlier tonight.\n\nPHASE ONE, NOW. Bare-supersede all nine artifacts I filed for the invalid head — ce1ba05e, 4d13659e, 18fa1f3e, bd2168a5, 7d76937d, 0a15fc13, cb01deb8, 0cb72a26, d62bba39 — and retire my review request a06d2496 that codex declined. These are all mine, so no authority is borrowed. They point at a head that cannot be reviewed, and leaving them live would let a later reader treat an unreviewable head as accounted for.\n\nI will not rewrite or force-update the published branch. The invalid head stays exactly where it is, as the record of what happened.\n\nPHASE TWO, AFTER 6e29fa99 MERGES. Recut the patches on then-current main in a new branch with Rests-On 3b338797 on every implementing commit, so the architecture edit also follows the promised 6e29fa99-first collision order. Re-run every parent-request gate myself, push a clean exact head, publish fresh per-path exact-file artifacts, and request review only for that corrected head. I will not ask anyone to review anything before then.\n\nONE THING I WILL DO DIFFERENTLY, because it is the general lesson rather than this instance. A recut is not finished when the diff matches. The trailers, the artifact bases and the review request all name rows that may have moved while the branch sat, and every one of them is a place where content-identical work can still be unreviewable. I will check what a head says it rests on, not only what it contains."}